{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_16010ea108571dcb7a1d265fd945fe8ae46bc81d8f684e5b1dc761a0613afeb9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"vinhnx/vtcode@18f7d26c76e2 snapshot d83edd9c49fa70e2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_36ca04af144d8dbb97e7ac702e325816b067ada6ef254a0bad1ebfeef01e33ef","slc_e130fb059d7d72bfab7b19917172d3f48a14de79e27b374d596245c1353978eb"],"source_ids":["src_8f7d27a517cb545db73607c1d4b75f5f"],"text":"VT Code is described as a secure, open-source terminal coding agent written in Rust, shipped as a single static binary for interactive and long-running autonomous work.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_162178fbb2ce931ce2e8e56772ac5136101131a67ab3b9465378587ac3b73c5c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"vinhnx/vtcode@18f7d26c76e2 snapshot d83edd9c49fa70e2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5c7d2faeec251c9969d2b63cbe4dfce87e4b682e8964dd07a6567107cd21970b","slc_649252cd18a97b668228f5465396d1a733018a244b81811c678f247d295b0422"],"source_ids":["src_5774b46e756b59c487a8c1654de38cd9"],"text":"Interactive sessions live-reload watched config changes with debouncing; safe settings apply without restart, and malformed edits keep the last valid configuration with a warning.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1e3bec124a4f73f70cdf323253c0b20a1b3e5515deefecf78676e391cf00e36a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"vinhnx/vtcode@18f7d26c76e2 snapshot d83edd9c49fa70e2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8a21dd0cc1da4794db55471751738b07ef1d1679e95d95daaffbaae9d3e287b8"],"source_ids":["src_9bc7d5b495a655f68373ea3e83f82d48"],"text":"Default public tool surface includes exec_command (shell via policy/sandbox/approvals), write_stdin for live-session continuation, and apply_patch with workspace-boundary checks.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_48a6b59da80c47ab9878bd8c7835334964a4fd640576244c5919012c21f24dc0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"vinhnx/vtcode@18f7d26c76e2 snapshot d83edd9c49fa70e2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0e7ed3914acbcea1ac24c94cc6fa082e1a1d640fc7b111a6651e74c1384058bb","slc_3498a156e7cdc70219eb88cbea450063f7c01fa28e3b9efca905ed94466bf6bd"],"source_ids":["src_8f7d27a517cb545db73607c1d4b75f5f","src_9bc7d5b495a655f68373ea3e83f82d48"],"text":"ThreadEvent (vtcode-exec-events) is the authoritative runtime event contract feeding replay, checkpoints, memory, and trajectory export; follow-up inputs queue and inject one at a time at idle boundaries.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_60046b34315663cfb147fe9d6b65a77b114c523287e08877ed52c61fda45c7d6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"vinhnx/vtcode@18f7d26c76e2 snapshot d83edd9c49fa70e2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5c5e24880780e8da23e1f5f6c55f9ac176751b31bac4ecc3e23d102692b6dd17","slc_dbc3dd6fa979e00f0ba56e53e809b8da56dfd5ee4be2208c0616c098ec082cf0"],"source_ids":["src_9bc7d5b495a655f68373ea3e83f82d48"],"text":"Delegation is modeled as explicit thread spawning: child agents do bounded sidecar work, their output is advisory until the parent validates and merges it into the SessionMemoryEnvelope at turn boundaries.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_663bfe81efe3364e76cb4773e59ac35b9d050340db2ddc8ec8612fe76ca3cd33","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"vinhnx/vtcode@18f7d26c76e2 snapshot d83edd9c49fa70e2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e755fccbddfe91301646b5c54c3bcfe834482fac4f0754c18de41bde73059f02","slc_ef84115347a23a17659d48b19ac9448dcbbde324392e5604eac19ee3a133b5ce"],"source_ids":["src_5774b46e756b59c487a8c1654de38cd9"],"text":"Configuration uses vtcode.toml at workspace or platform config-directory layers, with environment-variable overrides and a legacy $VTCODE_HOME path kept as a migration source.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6e5dbab108180acb00e3375600d1ea7b54fd606a3842be6720d12cccf0297428","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"vinhnx/vtcode@18f7d26c76e2 snapshot d83edd9c49fa70e2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1c65edfad8185d067da11dd848b28ca44ecbb933132fa5e765ac58c48a50d6a1","slc_54e61181b2465da6a2de2586781fe19caa9fea734278433067f7f2f5d9a48e83"],"source_ids":["src_8f7d27a517cb545db73607c1d4b75f5f","src_9bc7d5b495a655f68373ea3e83f82d48"],"text":"The architecture separates the model (reasoning) from the harness (runtime supplying tools, context, sandboxing, state, and verification), organized as seven reinforcing subsystems.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6ef343e7928a4cf6ae926150393063eea497ee91f908e4d7e43fef9a518d0da1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"vinhnx/vtcode@18f7d26c76e2 snapshot d83edd9c49fa70e2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_be888c6362ce48c9a4412ce117604ce993e9950258578fe5f45e40ca734063a3"],"source_ids":["src_9bc7d5b495a655f68373ea3e83f82d48"],"text":"The CLI separates data on stdout from diagnostics on stderr, uses clap for argument parsing, isolates subcommands (ask, exec, chat) in dedicated modules, and handles SIGINT/SIGTERM gracefully.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7f3c0cc587b459a327597326855b28aedbc7c126ef8e0074808864109c192089","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"vinhnx/vtcode@18f7d26c76e2 snapshot d83edd9c49fa70e2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_50c5e114c1c2448005189b6479c33f78a16554c163c11f54042327682c9c5e3f","slc_5c5e24880780e8da23e1f5f6c55f9ac176751b31bac4ecc3e23d102692b6dd17"],"source_ids":["src_9bc7d5b495a655f68373ea3e83f82d48"],"text":"A persisted SessionMemoryEnvelope summarizes objective, constraints, touched files, grounded facts, verification status, and delegated findings for resume and summarized-fork handoff.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8273e1126f3d9d7e38cf1b03c1ba2438054b74ed3c5244b458a991fc86deda54","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"vinhnx/vtcode@18f7d26c76e2 snapshot d83edd9c49fa70e2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2d90cf7ce1e5077bf01c5dceea3555dadeea640f19a23433e23796fe78b398a9"],"source_ids":["src_8f7d27a517cb545db73607c1d4b75f5f"],"text":"The README states the project is in active development and that local inference and some automation flows are experimental and may change between releases.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","created_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_a30db75e4cf6eaa56af6b0f0b2b3580641747e16e5690c7ce11bacaf859a410a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"vinhnx/vtcode@18f7d26c76e2 snapshot d83edd9c49fa70e2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9517c0ec4eab67dad8fea48bbf11547e42499b7188f4974523d0e2a65a9a4a31","slc_c38a17a13af176c37622b47d0179249ef908d432e849934bd5130d06c091e750"],"source_ids":["src_9bc7d5b495a655f68373ea3e83f82d48"],"text":"With agent.harness.orchestration_mode = plan_build_evaluate, a planner writes spec/contract artifacts, the generator runs on the main session, and an evaluator performs a skeptical post-build pass; failed evaluation triggers bounded revision rounds.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:21:46Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d7081122d750425fa14073511dacc7bc"}
